{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "f44159e5-7d8d-8db8-b569-b7eaa5541289",
  "created_at": "2026-01-06T15:17:51-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Timothy Gardiner",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Greg Lombardi",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:14:07-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Greg."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:14:10-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yeah. Finally a human. I've been through the phone menu so many times I'm on a first-name basis with it. Anyway, I've got a question about a deck permit."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:14:21-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry about that. Sure, go ahead. What's the project?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:14:25-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So I've got a deck out back, and a bunch of the boards are rotted. I'm just replacing the boards. Not building anything new. Does that count as new construction?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:14:36-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So you're pulling off the old decking and putting new boards on the same frame, same size, same footprint?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:14:44-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Same everything. Same size, same spot. Just the top boards. Maybe a couple of the railing pieces too, if they're bad."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:14:52-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Generally, straight like-for-like replacement of the surface boards is treated as repair, not new construction. Where it gets different is if you touch the framing, the posts, the footings, or change the size or height."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:15:05-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, but how do I know that? Like, is that written down somewhere or is that just what you're telling me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:15:13-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's how the building office generally looks at it. If you want it in writing, you can have someone in the inspections office confirm it for your specific property. I can put a note in or you can stop by."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:15:27-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hm. So no permit for the boards, but maybe a permit if the joists are bad. Did I get that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:15:35-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Close. Structural pieces, joists, beams, posts, ledger board, that's where a permit usually comes in. Boards and fasteners, usually not."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:15:43-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "What about the railing? I said a couple pieces. Is that structural?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:15:48-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Railings matter because of safety, height and spacing. Swapping a few balusters like for like is one thing. Rebuilding whole sections is another. If you're replacing a lot of it, call before you start."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:16:00-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Another thing. If I do need the permit, does a licensed contractor have to apply for it? Or can I do it myself?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:16:09-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "For a homeowner doing work on their own house, you can generally apply yourself. If you hire a contractor, then they'd normally pull it. Either way, the person doing the work has to be the one named."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:16:22-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wait, so if I apply myself, I'm the one doing the work. I can't have my buddy do it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:16:29-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, that's the catch. If a friend does the work, it gets murky. Best to bring that question to the office when you come in, and they'll tell you how it works."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:16:41-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I'm still a little confused on that one, honestly. So the contractor has to be licensed if they apply, but I don't if it's me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:16:50-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Correct. A contractor applying needs to be licensed. A homeowner applying for their own home, working on it themselves, doesn't."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:16:58-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. And this is for twenty-four Ocean Avenue, if that matters. Is there something on file for the deck already?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:17:06-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can't pull the whole record while we're talking. If you want, I'll leave a note on that address asking someone to look at it and call you back. Do you have a number?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:17:18-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, it's four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-nine-two."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:17:21-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-nine-two. And the name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:17:25-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Timothy Gardiner. G-A-R-D-I-N-E-R."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:17:27-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, Mr. Gardiner. I'll note it's about replacing deck boards at twenty-four Ocean, and whether the work needs a permit."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:17:35-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So just to double-check, boards only, no permit. Anything under it, yes permit. Right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:17:41-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's the general rule, yes. Someone will confirm for your address."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:17:46-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright, thanks. I'll wait for the call."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T15:17:49-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You bet. Take care."
    }
  ],
